{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Wool and linen together.</b> Because harm comes through both of them, they were forbidden to be worn together: Hevel brought from the firstborn of his flock; Cain brought from flax seed. Another interpretation: because from both of them are priestly garments, He warned them not to wear them in ordinary life, but only for His servants at the time of their service. And therefore a nega is found only in a wool garment or a linen garment, to show that there is transgression in kil'ayim. The verse restored it (spelled it out) to teach you that שעטנז is wool and linen."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:48.205836592Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}